  "question": {
    "text": "Let an ellipse with centre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and latus rectum of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> have its major axis along x-axis. If its minor axis subtends an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math> at the foci, then the square of the sum of the lengths of its minor and major axes is equal to _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>An ellipse with centre <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and latus rectum of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> have its major axis along x-axis&nbsp;</p><p>And its minor axis subtends an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math> at the foci,&nbsp;</p><p>So, on plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/12178a13-1713-4adc-91fc-6e84b5897480.png\" style=\"width: 340px; height: 256px;\" /></p><p>Now from diagram we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>a</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>tan</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now from equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
